Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: describe hims,h432b-braille
Upstream-Status: Pending

Describe required device resources separately from board wiring, with
explicit supplies and GPIO roles for validation of the runtime device tree.

---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/auxdisplay/hims,h432b-braille.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/auxdisplay/hims,h432b-braille.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: H432B 32-cell braille shift-register display
+
+maintainers:
+  - Freya Fractal <24643711+highenergymagic@users.noreply.github.com>
+
+description: |
+  Board display wiring with a 256-bit shift chain and separate cell-drive
+  enable. The neutral-frame and rail-settling sequence is part of this
+  board interface. This is not a generic SPI or SoC display controller.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    oneOf:
+      - const: hims,h432b-braille
+      - const: fractal,h432b-braille
+        deprecated: true
+
+  enable-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Active-high cell-drive enable.
+
+  data-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Active-high shift-register data input.
+
+  clock-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Active-high shift-register clock.
+
+  latch-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Active-high frame latch.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - enable-gpios
+  - data-gpios
+  - clock-gpios
+  - latch-gpios
+
+additionalProperties: false
